---
// Reference / CLI / changelog.
//
// Written rather than generated: the binary's own surface.
//
// No release contents are quoted here. The command's whole point is that the
// binary carries its own notes, so a page that transcribed them would be the
// one copy able to go stale.
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CliBlock from '../../../components/docs/CliBlock.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  editPath="src/pages/docs/reference/changelog.astro"
  title="changelog"
  description="What shipped, according to the binary you are holding, offline."
  section="Reference"
>
  <h1>changelog</h1>
  <p>
    <code>strata changelog</code> prints the release notes carried inside the binary. No network, and
    no chance of reading notes for a different version than the one installed.
  </p>
  <CliBlock>strata changelog</CliBlock>
  <p>One release at a time, when you know which one you care about:</p>
  <CliBlock>strata changelog --version 1.2.0</CliBlock>

  <h2>Why this is a command and not a link</h2>
  <p>
    The question it answers is usually "what changed between the version I had and the version I
    have now", and that is asked on a machine where the answer is already installed. Reading notes
    from a website adds a way to get it wrong: the page describes the newest release, which is not
    necessarily yours.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pair it with <a href="/docs/reference/doctor">doctor</a>, which tells you which version you are
    actually running, and with <a href="/docs/reference/update-and-uninstall">update --check</a>,
    which tells you whether there is a newer one.
  </p>

  <h2>Scripting it</h2>
  <p>
    <code>--json</code> returns the same content as a document, which is what to use when something else
    has to decide whether an upgrade is worth taking.
  </p>
  <CliBlock>strata --json changelog --version 1.2.0</CliBlock>
  <p>
    An unknown version is an error rather than empty output, so a typo in a script fails rather than
    quietly reporting that nothing changed. The error names every version this build documents,
    which is also the quickest way to see how far back its notes go.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
